## Intuition
To repeatedly reduce a number to a single digit, we first need a way to compute the sum of its digits.
This problem can be simplified by separating digit summation from repetition control, making the logic easy to follow and read.


## Approach

Use a recursive helper function to compute the sum of digits of a number.

Use a while loop to repeat the digit-sum operation until the result becomes a single digit.

This avoids pure recursion for better easy readability and clearer control flow.

## Solution
