## Complexity
Time Complexity: O(d), where d is the number of digits.
Space Complexity: O(d), due to recursion in digit summation.

## Intuition
The key observation is that we need to keep adding the digits of num until only one digit remains.

## Approach
1. Check whether `num` has more than one digit using:
   `while (num >= 10)`

2. Create a variable `sum = 0` to store the sum of the digits.

3. Use another loop to process every digit:
   `while (num > 0)`

4. Extract the last digit using:
   `int digit = num % 10;`

5. Add the digit to `sum`:
   `sum += digit;`

6. Remove the last digit:
   `num /= 10;`

7. After all digits have been processed, assign the sum back to `num`:
   `num = sum;`

8. Repeat the process until `num` becomes a single digit.

9. Finally, return `num`.

For a single-digit input such as `7`, the outer loop does not execute because `7 < 10`, so `7` is returned directly.


## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public int addDigits(int num) {
        //your code goes here
        while (num >= 10) {

            int sum = 0;

            while (num > 0) {
                int digit = num % 10;
                sum += digit;
                num /= 10;
            }

            num = sum;
        }

        return num;
    }
}
```

